  "tagline": "PostgreSQL-based continuous-query analytics engine from Berkeley's Telegraph project; bought by Cisco in 2012.",
  "description": "Truviso was a Foster City startup founded in 2006 by UC Berkeley professor Michael Franklin and Sailesh Krishnamurthy to commercialise the TelegraphCQ stream-processing research. Its TruCQ engine extended PostgreSQL with always-on SQL queries over data streams, joined against stored tables, so results updated as events arrived instead of after batch loads; a web-analytics application followed in 2010. Cisco acquired the company on May 4, 2012 and absorbed the technology, ending Truviso as a product. Its ideas resurfaced in PipelineDB and in today's streaming SQL databases.",
